§ `Imaginary Alcohol Act (record spelling)`

-- The SEMANTIC TWIN of `alcohol.l4`: the same three provisions, the same
-- decisions under the same names, spelled with `DECLARE` records instead of
-- top-level `ASSUME`.
--
-- Its job is the oracle. `ASSUME` is uninterpreted, so `l4 run` cannot evaluate
-- a decision in `alcohol.l4`, and `lowerQuery` builds a scenario only out of a
-- record-literal query argument — so an `#EVAL` there would lower to a query
-- with no facts. An ASSUME-shaped seed ships no evaluable directive, and
-- pairing its zero oracles against its zero tests is a VACUOUS green: a pass
-- reported having executed nothing.
--
-- Every record below is named exactly as the corresponding `ASSUME`d TYPE in
-- `alcohol.l4`, and every field exactly as the corresponding `ASSUME` —
-- character for character, in the same order. The two files therefore mangle to
-- the SAME s(CASP) atoms at the SAME arities, and `etc/blawx-tier1-harness.py`
-- runs each `#EVAL` below twice: against this file's workspaces, and with the
-- same fact rows replayed against `alcohol.l4`'s. The `-- L4 oracle ==>` value
-- measured here is the single expectation for both. Do not "tidy" the field
-- names; they are an interface.
--
-- Measured on this tree, the two emitted `.pl` streams are byte-identical
-- except for the provenance comment naming the source file — so "one logic,
-- two spellings" is a measurement here, not a claim.
--
-- ONE THING THE TWIN CANNOT SHOW, and it is the point of the pair: under R5 a
-- boolean RECORD FIELD and an `ASSUME`d input both emit the signed unary goal,
-- so the epistemics agree — but only the `ASSUME` side is a module that a
-- lawyer could have written without inventing a data structure first. The twin
-- exists to anchor the numbers, not to replace the seed.

DECLARE Person HAS
    `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person engages in business for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a public house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has an unspent conviction for fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has an alcohol banning order` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Premises HAS
    `a price list for alcohol is displayed on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are registered as a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the enforcement officer believes that the price list is misleading to customers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the enforcement officer has issued a warning to the proprietor of premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor corrects the price list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor does so to the satisfaction of the enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proprietor does so within 5 days after the warning was issued` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Imaginary Alcohol Act ss (1)-(2): a body corporate engaging in business for profit, other than a public house or a hotel, must not sell alcohol if it has an unspent conviction for fraud, or an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment, or an alcohol banning order.
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must not sell alcohol` IF
        p's `the person is a body corporate`
    AND p's `the person engages in business for profit`
    AND NOT p's `the person is a public house`
    AND NOT p's `the person is a hotel`
    AND (    p's `the person has an unspent conviction for fraud`
          OR p's `the person has an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment`
          OR p's `the person has an alcohol banning order`)

@export Imaginary Alcohol Act s (3): where a price list for alcohol is displayed on premises registered as a hotel and the enforcement officer believes the list is misleading to customers, the officer may issue a warning to the proprietor of the premises.
GIVEN pr IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enforcement officer may issue a warning to the proprietor of premises` IF
        pr's `a price list for alcohol is displayed on the premises`
    AND pr's `the premises are registered as a hotel`
    AND pr's `the enforcement officer believes that the price list is misleading to customers`

@export Imaginary Alcohol Act s (4): where a warning has been issued and it is not the case that the proprietor corrected the price list, to the satisfaction of the enforcement officer, within 5 days after the warning was issued, the officer may cancel the registration of the hotel. All three limbs must hold for the proprietor to escape — correcting the list late, or to nobody's satisfaction, leaves the registration cancellable.
GIVEN pr IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the enforcement officer may cancel the registration of the hotel` IF
        pr's `the enforcement officer has issued a warning to the proprietor of premises`
    AND NOT (    pr's `the proprietor corrects the price list`
             AND pr's `the proprietor does so to the satisfaction of the enforcement officer`
             AND pr's `the proprietor does so within 5 days after the warning was issued`)

-- q1: a body corporate trading for profit, neither pub nor hotel, with an unspent fraud conviction
#EVAL `the person must not sell alcohol`
        (Person WITH `the person is a body corporate` IS TRUE,
                     `the person engages in business for profit` IS TRUE,
                     `the person is a public house` IS FALSE,
                     `the person is a hotel` IS FALSE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for fraud` IS TRUE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment` IS FALSE,
                     `the person has an alcohol banning order` IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> TRUE

-- q2: the same body, but a hotel -- ss (1)-(2) does not reach it
#EVAL `the person must not sell alcohol`
        (Person WITH `the person is a body corporate` IS TRUE,
                     `the person engages in business for profit` IS TRUE,
                     `the person is a public house` IS FALSE,
                     `the person is a hotel` IS TRUE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for fraud` IS TRUE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment` IS FALSE,
                     `the person has an alcohol banning order` IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q3: the same body, but a public house -- the other carve-out
#EVAL `the person must not sell alcohol`
        (Person WITH `the person is a body corporate` IS TRUE,
                     `the person engages in business for profit` IS TRUE,
                     `the person is a public house` IS TRUE,
                     `the person is a hotel` IS FALSE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for fraud` IS TRUE,
                     `the person has an unspent conviction for providing misleading information in relation to an application for a licence under an enactment` IS FALSE,
                     `the person has an alcohol banning order` IS FALSE)
-- L4 oracle ==> FALSE

-- q4: the second conviction limb -- misleading information on a licence application
#EVAL `the person must not sell alcohol`
        (Person WITH `the person is a body corporate` IS TRUE,
